        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1f9cc037-f9bf-56ce-baf6-2321bb82deb7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Morgan Paull, Hampton Fancher, David Peoples, Philip K. Dick\n- Works: Blade Runner, Do Androids Dream of Electric Sheep?, Dirty O'Neil\n- Roles: Dave Holden, Jimmy O'Neil\n- Places: Texas\n\nFacts:\n- Philip K. Dick wrote the 1968 novel \"Do Androids Dream of Electric Sheep?\"\n- \"Blade Runner\" was scripted by Hampton Fancher and David Peoples as a loose adaptation of Philip K. Dick’s 1968 novel \"Do Androids Dream of Electric Sheep?\"\n- Morgan Paull was an American actor born on December 15, 1944, and he died on July 17, 2012.\n- Morgan Paull was most notable for playing Dave Holden in Ridley Scott’s film \"Blade Runner.\"\n- In \"Dirty O'Neil,\" Morgan Paull played Jimmy O'Neil, a cop in a small Texas town with a fondness for women.\n- In \"Dirty O'Neil,\" Jimmy O'Neil is forced into action when three homicidal thugs invade the town.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
